title Caravan understudy -- a record may carry two shapes of one phase at once
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; send each finished increment
think Standfast first. Every REDS row read closed -- 81, 82, 83, 84, 85 (reopened and closed), 86, 87 -- and memory is not measurement, so I ran the two living-card guards on metal rather than trusting the ledger. living_card_ascii_witness GREEN; the e123 living-pin guard GREEN (its witness lives at tools/gen/season/, not tools/, which cost one FileNotFound before I looked). No open agent-closable red, so constructive work may begin.
think Council rota, lap index 39 rings mod 27 = 12: active-designing/20260618-184912_growing-a-language.md. Its five moves are exactly what this arc does each rung -- stand on proven ground, wear a thin costume, own the core by path, diverge by strengthening rather than rewriting, dogfood and gate. And the line that governs this lap: a complex system that works grew from a simpler system that worked.
think The running thread names its own next crux. The 20260819.211527 log and replace.rye both close on the same open question -- whether a run may correct a phase a child is RUNNING, letting the work in flight finish under the shape it started with while the record already reads the new one. Lindy-first crux-first picks it: the highest-Lindy work here is the invariant, and this is the hardest still-tractable move in the arc.
think Named it before building it, under the Comlink tendency -- clearest, most fun, safest word. Understudy: the elder plays out its scene while the newcomer waits in the wings, which is exactly the shape. Grepped the whole tree; understudy collides with nothing.
think Read the readings before designing. commute.admissible weighs the head against live children by their captured domain; elder_waits, sibling_waits, and may_pass each skip a phase that is not waiting; judge_outcome reads the Finished struct captured at spawn. So the separation the rung needs already exists -- the finding is that the door costs nothing, rather than that it needs new machinery.
think What the run genuinely lacks is a memory of which slot each live child came from. Without it a record cannot tell a phase still in flight from a phase already home, and those two want opposite answers. Added from[max_in_flight] to the Table, set at admission and shifted with live on every reaping.
think Two refusals earned, and I resisted folding them. UnderstudyMoved is about place -- a running phase's step is already spent, and enlist.rye's lesson (a run must never forget what it spent) says a moved shape would leave one turn missing a step it ran and another holding a step it never started. UnderstudyHomed is about time -- rewriting finished work makes the record lie about what ran. One about place, one about time.
think Generalization test, this arc's standing habit: hand the door a waiting phase and every answer comes from replace.rye, refusal for refusal. Wrote it as a walk of all seven phases comparing both doors by error name, since a phase whose turn a follower names is refused by both -- requiring both to admit would have been the wrong claim.
obs The first cut of the seating refusal panicked rather than refusing: a shape for turn 0 naming turn 6 violates turns_are_sound, so plan_is_seated asserts instead of answering false. The lap's queue writes turn 0 through turn 6 in that very order, so no turn a phase may lawfully name ever stands after it -- the refusal is unreachable there. Built a two-phase reordered record putting a low turn last on purpose, which is what makes ReplacementUnseated reachable at all. The metal named the gap; I did not reason it out first.
obs All three RED paths proven on metal before the claim. Judging the reaped child from table.record[table.from[0]] rather than from table.live[0] reds at "client_a: expected bytes differed, heard carried" -- the finding shown as a failure, since the swapped shape owes a different outcome. Dropping the place refusal seats a moved shape. Dropping the running check rewrites a phase already home.
obs Docs-implementation-sync applied in the same round: replace.rye's README section claimed the running question "belongs to the vision room until a witness binds it," and a witness now binds it. That sentence now points at the rung below, and the Understudy section stands beside it.
loom witness=caravan_understudy_witness result=GREEN understudy_tests=19 replace_tests=32 seating_tests=256 turns_forgotten_understudy=0 turns_forgotten_move=2 places=7 children=7 carried_home=2 shapes_swapped=1 named_turns_broken=0
